I think this (the chosen values) is the main point where we
disagree.

In my experience, it is fairly common to have 20-30 potions
that could be alchemized to full healing potions once you've
made it through the main dungeon (down the to castle.)  Even
with the stack size limits that you suggested, I think that a
typical player with the gain level / gain energy / speed
potions that you'll find as well will be able to usually
alchemize most of their potions into full healing, and so gain
150+ max HP, as well as having some left over for emergency
healing.  I think that's way too much.

As I mentioned before, I think that color alchemy probably
helps somewhat, as it's generally going to reduce the chance
that very desirable potions can be alchemized from common
ones.  It will be highly variable, though -- and sometimes
other potions besides full healing will be available in large
quantities.

If building off of your suggestion that large stacks will
explode, I would want to see stacks larger than maybe 3
explode.  If people are adamant that there should be a chance
that larger stacks succeed, then I would suggest something
like the following chances for failure:

1 or 2 potions: 0%
3: 10%
4: 50%
5: 75%
6+: 100%

This would make it much more difficult to make huge stacks of
potions, but it still should be possible to create a few if
you need them.  I do think that would be a good change,
regardless of anything else done to alchemy.

